<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LanguageData>
  
  <!-- EN: deep devotion -->
  <AM_DeepDevotion.label>地底敬献</AM_DeepDevotion.label>
  <!-- EN: Humans ought to live underground, and enjoy the succulent fruit of the depths.\n<color=#c79fef>Extreme version of the Tunneler meme.</color> -->
  <AM_DeepDevotion.description>人类必须生活在神圣的地下，享受地下深处最为甜美多汁的果实。\n\n&lt;color=#c79fef>这是“地底之心”模因更极端化的版本。&lt;/color></AM_DeepDevotion.description>
  <!-- EN:
    <li>creation(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)        ->Before the mountains rose and the seas were formed, [deity0_name] carved the first chamber from the living earth. There [deity0_pronoun] sheltered the first people and taught them that the world above was never meant to be their home.</li>
    <li>episode(uses=1,tag=meme_DeepDevotion)  ->When [deity0_possessive] people had exhausted the riches of the upper earth, [deity0_name] opened a passage into the depths and revealed the endless bounty hidden beneath their feet.</li>
    <li>intro(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)           ->When the first settlers reached the [place_summary] [place_name], they were afraid of the endless sky above them. The [deity0_type] [deity0_name] answered their prayers by revealing a great cavern beneath the earth.</li>
    <li>conflict(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)        ->A proud [foeLeader] mocked the [memberNamePlural] for hiding beneath the earth, claiming that true people belonged beneath the open sky. The faithful answered by digging deeper.</li>
    <li>founderJoin(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->[founderName] spent seven years alone in a cave beneath [place_name], surviving on fungus and water. When [founderName] emerged, [founder_pronoun] proclaimed that the deepest darkness had shown [founder_objective] the true meaning of life.</li>
    <li>victory(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)         ->When the [foeLeader] invaded the [memberNamePlural]' settlement, [founderName] ordered everyone to retreat underground. The invaders found nothing but empty rooms, while the [memberNamePlural] emerged from hidden tunnels behind them and drove them away.</li>
    <li>setup(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)           ->[founderName] looked upon the vastness of the surface and saw only emptiness. Beneath the earth, surrounded by stone, [founderName] discovered purpose and founded our movement.</li>
    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_DeepDevotion)    ->[founderName] gathered those who feared the surface and led them into the mountains. Together they carved halls, chambers, and sanctuaries from the rock, creating a home that could never be taken from them.</li>
    <li>lessonIntro(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)         ->I once climbed to the surface and looked upon the endless sky. That was when I understood:</li>
    <li>lesson(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)              ->the farther we descend beneath the earth, the closer we come to the place where humanity truly belongs</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_DeepDevotion) ->Do not fear the darkness. The stone above us is stronger than any sky.</li>
    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)    ->The archotechs understood that survival requires control over one's environment. They buried their greatest works beneath the earth, where neither weather nor the stars could interfere.</li>
    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->The archotechs constructed vast subterranean complexes capable of sustaining entire populations without ever requiring access to the surface.</li>
    <li>archistProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion) ->[inTheEnd], the surface will become an abandoned ruin while the archotechs awaken beneath the earth to welcome those who followed their example.</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->The earth remembers every footstep taken upon it. Those who dwell beneath the soil can hear its ancient memories in the silence.</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->Every stone has a spirit, but the oldest stones possess the greatest wisdom. We must dig deep enough to hear them.</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->The roots of the great trees reach downward seeking the same ancient spirits that dwell in the deep earth.</li>
    <li>serketistProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->[itIsSaid] that the sacred insects were the first creatures to discover the hidden passages beneath the earth, and that they still guard the deepest chambers.</li>
    <li>chthonianProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->Something ancient sleeps beneath the lowest stone. Those who descend far enough may hear it breathing in the darkness.</li>
    <li>esotericismProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->Every layer of earth conceals another layer of reality. Those who descend far enough will eventually reach the truth beneath existence itself.</li>
    <li>eschatologismFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->When the final age arrives, the mountains will close over the world and the last survivors will retreat into the eternal depths, where they will wait for the surface to die.</li>
    <li>introMemo(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->Management is pleased to announce the completion of our new Deep Workplace Optimization Initiative. Employees are encouraged to relocate their desks, meetings, cafeterias, break rooms, and personal quarters to increasingly lower floors. Studies indicate that employee satisfaction increases by approximately 4% for every hundred meters below ground.</li>
    <li>alienistProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->Humanity has spent its history looking toward the stars, but perhaps the greatest civilizations are those that turned inward and built their worlds beneath the surface.</li>
  -->
  <AM_DeepDevotion.descriptionMaker.rules.rulesStrings>
    <li>creation(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)        ->在群山隆起、大海形成之前，[deity0_name]便在生机盎然的地底开辟了首个住所。在那里， [deity0_pronoun]为第一批子民提供了庇护，并告诫他们：地表世界从来都不是他们的家园。</li>
    <li>episode(uses=1,tag=meme_DeepDevotion)  ->当[deity0_possessive]子民们耗尽了地表的丰富资源时，[deity0_name]开启了通往地底深处的道路，并揭示了埋藏在他们脚下的无尽宝物。</li>
    <li>intro(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)           ->当首批定居者抵达[place_summary][place_name]时，他们惧怕头顶无垠的苍穹。[deity0_type][deity0_name]回应了他们的祈祷，在大地之下揭露了一个巨大的洞穴。</li>
    <li>conflict(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)        ->一名傲慢的[foeLeader]嘲笑[memberNamePlural]躲藏在地下，并声称真正的人类应当生活在广阔的天空之下。作为回应，信徒们更加卖力地挥动起了挖掘工具。</li>
    <li>founderJoin(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->[founderName]在[place_name]下方的洞穴中独自生活了七年，以菌菇和水为生。当[founderName]走出洞穴时，[founder_pronoun]对外宣告：至深的黑暗已向[founder_objective]展示了生命的真正意义。</li>
    <li>victory(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)         ->当[foeLeader]侵入[memberNamePlural]的定居点时，[founderName]命令所有人撤入地下。入侵者们只找到空无一人的房间，而[memberNamePlural]则从他们身后的密道中现身，将他们赶走。</li>
    <li>setup(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)           ->[founderName]望向辽阔的地面，却只看到了空虚。在大地之下，那被岩石环绕之处，[founderName]发现了目标，并确定了我们的反抗大业。</li>
    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_DeepDevotion)    ->[founderName]将那些惧怕地表的人聚集在一起，带领他们深入群山。他们一同从岩石中凿出大厅、密室与圣所，创造了一个永远无法被夺走的家园。</li>
    <li>lessonIntro(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)         ->我曾爬上地表，望向无垠的苍穹。就在那时，我明白了：</li>
    <li>lesson(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)              ->我们越深入地下，就越接近人类真正的归属之地</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_DeepDevotion) ->不要惧怕黑暗。我们头顶的岩石，比任何天空都要坚固。</li>
    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)    ->超凡智能知晓生存需要先掌控自身环境。祂将最伟大的作品埋藏于大地之下，在那里，无论是天气还是星辰都无法干扰。</li>
    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->超凡智能建造了庞大的地下建筑群，足以维持大量人口生存，而又无需接触地表。</li>
    <li>archistProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion) ->[inTheEnd]，地表将成为被遗弃的废墟，而超凡智能将在大地之下苏醒，迎接那些追随祂的人。</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->大地记得在其上走过的每一个脚步。那些居于土地之下的人，能在寂静中聆听它古老的记忆。</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->每块岩石都拥有灵魂，但最古老的岩石拥有最伟大的智慧。我们必须挖得足够深，才能听见它们。</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)     ->参天大树之根向下蔓延，寻找着同样栖居于地下深处的古老灵魂。</li>
    <li>serketistProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->[itIsSaid]，神圣的虫族是最早发现地下密道的生物，它们至今仍守护着最深的密室。</li>
    <li>chthonianProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->某种古老之物在最底层的岩石下沉眠。那些足够深入的人，或许能在黑暗中听见它的呼吸。</li>
    <li>esotericismProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->每一层大地都隐藏着另一层现实。那些足够深入的人，终将抵达隐藏于存在本身之下的真理。</li>
    <li>eschatologismFact(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->当终焉时代来临，群山将合拢覆盖世界，最后的生还者们将退入永恒的深处，在那里等待地表凋亡。</li>
    <li>introMemo(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->管理层很高兴向大家宣布，我们新的“深层工作场所优化倡议”已完成，鼓励员工将他们的办公桌、会议室、食堂、休息室和个人宿舍迁往越来越低的楼层。研究表明，在地下每深入一百米，员工满意度约提升4%。</li>
    <li>alienistProphecy(tag=meme_DeepDevotion)->人类自从有记载以来一直在仰望群星，但或许最伟大的文明，是那些转向内部、在地表之下建造世界的人。</li>
  </AM_DeepDevotion.descriptionMaker.rules.rulesStrings>
