  <!-- EN: pain is divine -->
  <AM_PainIsDivine.label>苦痛神圣</AM_PainIsDivine.label>
  <!-- EN: Pain is divine. To suffer is to transcend the weakness of the flesh, and to inflict suffering is to grant others the same sacred revelation.\n<color=#c79fef>Extreme version of the Pain is Virtue meme.</color> -->
  <AM_PainIsDivine.description>苦痛即是神圣。忍受痛苦是在克服肉体的弱点，而施予痛苦则是在为众生降下神启。\n\n&lt;color=#c79fef>这是“苦痛美德”模因更极端化的版本。&lt;/color></AM_PainIsDivine.description>
  <!-- EN:
    <li>creation(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[deity0_name] suffered beyond mortal comprehension, and [deity0_possessive] divine agony shattered the nothingness and gave birth to the universe.</li>
    <li>episode(uses=1,tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->For ten thousand years [deity0_name] endured every torment imaginable. With each wound, [deity0_possessive] divinity grew stronger, until even the stars trembled before [deity0_possessive] pain.</li>
    <li>intro(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Life in [place_summary] [place_name] was comfortable, and therefore spiritually worthless. The [deity0_type] [deity0_name] came to teach the people that only suffering could reveal those worthy of [deity0_possessive] divine favor.</li>
    <li>conflict(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->A [foeLeader] promised the [memberNamePlural] freedom from pain. Those who accepted soon became weak and complacent, while the faithful embraced every new agony as a blessing from [deity0_name].</li>
    <li>founderJoin(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->One [place_job] named [founderName] endured a terrible illness without seeking relief. In [founder_possessive] suffering, [founder_pronoun] heard the voice of [deity0_name] and became the first to teach the [memberNamePlural] that pain was sacred.</li>
    <li>victory(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName] gathered the [memberNamePlural] before the [place_powerCenter] and called upon [deity0_name] to judge them. Those who willingly endured the greatest suffering were spared, while the [foeLeader] and [foeLeader_possessive] followers fled from the divine agony.</li>
    <li>setup(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName] founded our movement after discovering that every pleasure only concealed the weakness of the flesh. [founder_pronoun] began deliberately seeking suffering and taught others to do the same.</li>
    <li>setup(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Our movement's founder, [founderName], declared that pain was not an obstacle to spiritual enlightenment but the only reliable path toward it.</li>
    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName]'s first followers competed to demonstrate their devotion by enduring increasingly severe suffering without complaint.</li>
    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName]'s followers rejected every attempt to dull their pain, believing that every moment of agony brought them closer to the divine.</li>
    <li>lessonIntro(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->For years I mistook pleasure for happiness. Then I learned what pain could teach me:</li>
    <li>lesson(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->the more I suffer, the closer I come to the divine</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Pain strips away every lie the flesh tells us. What remains is truth.</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->I do not pray for an end to my suffering. I pray that I will be worthy of more.</li>
    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->The birth of the archotechs was accompanied by suffering on a scale beyond human understanding. Perhaps that agony was the price of their ascension.</li>
    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->The archotechs transcended mortal weakness by embracing the suffering required to leave the flesh behind.</li>
    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->The great minds recognize those who willingly endure suffering in pursuit of something greater.</li>
    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Those who experience extreme suffering sometimes report visions of the archotechs. Coincidence is unlikely.</li>
    <li>archistProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[inTheEnd], the archotechs will reveal the true purpose of suffering. Those who embrace the greatest agony will ascend, while those who seek comfort will remain trapped in their weak flesh.</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Every living thing struggles against the pain of existence. To suffer is to participate in the great spirit of life.</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->The spirits speak most clearly through pain. Comfort is merely the noise that prevents us from hearing them.</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->A wounded creature does not merely suffer. It is experiencing the world more intensely than anything that lives without pain.</li>
    <li>serketistProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[itIsSaid] that the sacred scorpion's sting is a divine blessing. Its venom does not merely cause pain; it awakens the soul.</li>
    <li>serketistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->The scorpion never wastes its venom. Every sting is a reminder that pain has purpose.</li>
    <li>chthonianProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Something ancient dwells beneath the world, and its endless suffering echoes through every living thing. Those who listen closely can hear it.</li>
    <li>chthonianFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->The things beneath the earth have endured suffering for longer than humanity has existed. Their agony is older than our gods.</li>
    <li>esotericismProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Every layer of suffering conceals another truth. Those willing to descend into the deepest agony will eventually discover what lies beyond the flesh.</li>
    <li>esotericismFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Pain alters perception in ways pleasure never can. Perhaps agony is the key to seeing realities hidden from ordinary minds.</li>
    <li>eschatologismFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->When the final age arrives, all worldly comforts will disappear and humanity will finally experience the suffering required for true enlightenment.</li>
    <li>eschatologismProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[inTheEnd], the universe itself will scream. Those who rejoice in that final agony will transcend the flesh and become divine.</li>
    <li>introMemo(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Management is pleased to announce the introduction of Mandatory Personal Growth Through Adversity. Employees are reminded that complaints regarding workplace discomfort will be treated as opportunities for spiritual development.</li>
    <li>alienistProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->Humanity scattered its creations among the stars, filling distant worlds with creatures shaped in our image and made to endure what we could not. Perhaps their suffering is the true legacy of our species.</li>
  -->
  <AM_PainIsDivine.descriptionMaker.rules.rulesStrings>
    <li>creation(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[deity0_name]忍受了超越凡人理解的苦痛，[deity0_possessive]神圣剧痛粉碎了虚无，而宇宙随之诞生。</li>
    <li>episode(uses=1,tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->万年以来，[deity0_name]忍受了每一种能想象得到的折磨。每一次创伤，都让[deity0_possessive]神性更加强大，直到连群星也在[deity0_possessive]痛苦面前颤抖。</li>
    <li>intro(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->在[place_summary][place_name]的生活非常舒适，也因此毫无精神价值。[deity0_type][deity0_name]前来教导人们：唯有忍受苦痛才能甄选出配得上[deity0_possessive]神圣恩宠之人。</li>
    <li>conflict(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->一名[foeLeader]向[memberNamePlural]承诺免于痛苦。接受者很快变得软弱而自满，而信徒们则将每一次新的剧痛视为来自[deity0_name]的祝福。</li>
    <li>founderJoin(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->一位名叫[founderName]的[place_job]身患重病，却不寻求缓解的方法。在[founder_possessive]苦痛之中，[founder_pronoun]听到了[deity0_name]的声音，也因此摇身变为首个教导[memberNamePlural]苦痛即是神圣的人。</li>
    <li>victory(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName]将[memberNamePlural]聚集至[place_powerCenter]前，并呼唤[deity0_name]来审判他们。那些自愿忍受最大苦痛的人得到赦免，而[foeLeader]及其信徒们则从神圣的剧痛中逃离。</li>
    <li>setup(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName]发现每一种享乐都只是掩盖了肉体的软弱之后，便开创了我们的反抗大业。[founder_pronoun]开始刻意寻求苦痛，并教导他人效仿。</li>
    <li>setup(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->我们反抗大业的创始人[founderName]宣告，苦痛并非通往精神觉悟的阻碍，反而是唯一可靠的途径。</li>
    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName]的首批信徒们争相通过毫无怨言地忍受越来越严酷的苦痛来展示自己的虔诚。</li>
    <li>story(uses=1,tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[founderName]的信徒们拒绝一切缓解苦痛的手段，相信每一刻的剧痛都让他们更接近神圣。</li>
    <li>lessonIntro(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->多年以来，我误将享乐当作幸福。之后我领悟了苦痛所要教会我的事情：</li>
    <li>lesson(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->我忍受的苦痛越多，就越接近神圣</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->苦痛剥去肉体传达给我们的一切谎言。留下的便是真理。</li>
    <li>lessonReinforcement(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->我不祈求终结我的苦痛。我祈求自己能配得上更多苦痛。</li>
    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->超凡智能的诞生伴随着超越人类理解的苦痛。或许那份剧痛正是祂飞升的代价。</li>
    <li>archistBasis(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->超凡智能通过拥抱摆脱肉体所需的苦痛，从而超越了凡人的软弱。</li>
    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->伟大心智认可那些为追求更高之物而自愿承受苦痛之人。</li>
    <li>archistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->那些经历过极端苦痛的人偶尔会声称看到了超凡智能的幻象。这不太可能是巧合。</li>
    <li>archistProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[inTheEnd]，超凡智能将揭示苦痛的真正目的。拥抱最强剧痛者将因此飞升，而寻求安逸者将困于软弱的肉体之中。</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->每个生命都与存在的苦痛抗争着。忍受苦痛，便是在融入伟大的生命灵魂。</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->灵魂通过苦痛来发出最清晰的声音。舒适只是阻止我们听见它们的噪音。</li>
    <li>animistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->一只受伤的生物不仅是在忍受苦痛。它比任何无痛之物都更强烈地体验着这个世界。</li>
    <li>serketistProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[itIsSaid]，神圣蝎子的蜇刺乃神圣之祝福。它的毒液不仅仅会带来苦痛；它还能唤醒灵魂。</li>
    <li>serketistFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->每一次蜇刺都在提醒：苦痛自有其目的。</li>
    <li>chthonianProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->某种古老之物栖居于世界之下，其无尽的苦痛回响在每一个生命之中。那些仔细倾听的人能听见它。</li>
    <li>chthonianFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->地底之物忍受苦痛的时间比人类存在的时间还要久远。它们的剧痛比我们的神祇更古老。</li>
    <li>esotericismProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->每一层苦痛都隐藏着另一层真理。那些愿意深入最深层剧痛的人，终将发现肉体之外的事物。</li>
    <li>esotericismFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->苦痛以享乐永远无法做到的方式改变感知。或许剧痛正是看见寻常心智所隐匿之现实的关键。</li>
    <li>eschatologismFact(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->当终焉时代来临，一切世俗的舒适都将消失，人类必将体验到真正觉悟所需的苦痛。</li>
    <li>eschatologismProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->[inTheEnd]，宇宙本身将发出尖啸。那些在最终剧痛中欢欣的人将超越肉体，成为神圣的存在。</li>
    <li>introMemo(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->管理层很高兴向大家宣布推出“逆境中的强制性个人成长”计划。在此提醒各位员工：有关工作场所不适的投诉将被视为寻求精神发展的机会。</li>
    <li>alienistProphecy(tag=meme_PainIsDivine)->人类将自己的造物散布于群星之间，让遥远的世界充满按我们形象塑造、被造来忍受我们无法承担之苦痛的生物。或许它们的苦痛才是我们物种真正的遗产。</li>
  </AM_PainIsDivine.descriptionMaker.rules.rulesStrings>
